    ('180', '"I stopped by Bakehouse in Amerikamura, Osaka and tried a few treats. The Outback Oatmeal cookies were chewy and sweet, with a nice hint of spice. The Austin Almond Biscotti was crunchy and nutty, perfect for dipping in coffee. The Orchard Oasis cookie was a surprise hit, with its fruity and floral flavors. The Golden Gate Ginger and Tokyo Tidbits were just okay, lacking a bit of depth. The Pearly Pies, however, were a highlight - flaky crust and a sweet, creamy filling. Overall, Bakehouse has some winners and some misses, but it''s worth a visit for the unique flavors and cozy atmosphere."', '3000010', '2024-05-31T15:23:53.074Z');


